/*!  \page grib_parameters grib_parameters
\section DESCRIPTION
 Query parameter definitions in ecCodes concept files (GRIB edition 1 and 2)
 and print matching entries with paramId, shortName, name, units and optionally
 the GRIB encoding.
 \n
 The tool reads the concept files paramId.def, shortName.def, name.def and units.def
 below grib1/ and grib2/, including all localConcepts. For GRIB2 it also reads the
 variants used by the MTG2 switch: *.lte33.def (is_mtg2_switch=0), *.def (is_mtg2_switch=1)
 and *.chemsplit.def (is_mtg2_switch=2).
 \n
 Entries of the different concept files are joined into one record when edition,
 MTG2 switch, scope and encoding are identical. If several paramIds in the same scope
 have the same encoding, they are shown as a list, e.g. paramId=[500417, 500582].
 A value which is not defined for an encoding is shown as '-'.
 \n
 Which definitions are read: without --definitions-root, the tool uses the same
 definitions path as ecCodes, i.e. ECCODES_EXTRA_DEFINITION_PATH, then
 ECCODES_DEFINITION_PATH or the built-in default, which may be MEMFS. As in ecCodes,
 a definition file present in several directories is taken from the first one that
 has it. The output therefore shows what the installed ecCodes actually uses.

\section USAGE
 grib_parameters
 [options]
 \n
 Without options, a short usage text is printed. To list all entries, give any
 option, e.g. --format line.

\section OPTIONS
-h, --help  \n
        Show this help text and exit.
 \n \n --definitions-root path \n
        Definitions root directory, used instead of the ecCodes definitions path.
        Multiple paths can be supplied using the platform path separator
        (':' on Unix, ';' on Windows). A definition file present in several roots
        is taken from the first root that has it.
 \n \n --debug-path-resolution \n
        Print the ecCodes definitions path, the candidate and selected roots and the
        backend used (filesystem, memfs or mixed) to stderr. Also reports concept files
        read from disk which a MEMFS build would not find.
 \n \n --columns col1,col2,... \n
        Output only selected columns.
        Valid columns: edition,is_mtg2_switch,scope,paramId,shortName,name,units,encoding,sources
 \n \n --scope scope1,scope2,... \n
        Comma-separated list of exact scopes to include,
        e.g. grib2,grib2/localConcepts/ecmf. An unknown scope is reported together
        with the list of available scopes.
 \n \n --name pattern \n
        Wildcard filter for name (case-insensitive), e.g. '*precipitation*'.
 \n \n --name-regex regex \n
        Regex filter for name.
 \n \n --shortName pattern \n
        Wildcard filter for shortName (case-insensitive), e.g. '10*'.
 \n \n --shortName-regex regex \n
        Regex filter for shortName.
 \n \n --paramId pattern \n
        Wildcard filter for paramId.
 \n \n --paramId-regex regex \n
        Regex filter for paramId.
 \n \n --units pattern \n
        Wildcard filter for units (case-insensitive).
 \n \n --units-regex regex \n
        Regex filter for units.
 \n \n --regex-case-sensitive \n
        Make regex filters case-sensitive. By default they are case-insensitive.
 \n \n --attr key=value,key=value,... \n
        Filter by encoding. A record matches when its encoding contains at least
        the listed key/value pairs.
 \n \n --attr-strict \n
        With --attr and/or --attrkey, require an exact match: the encoding must have
        exactly the listed keys, with the values given in --attr.
 \n \n --attrkey key1,key2,... \n
        Keep only records whose encoding contains all listed keys, with any value.
 \n \n --nattrkey key1,key2,... \n
        Exclude records whose encoding contains any of the listed keys.
 \n \n --nattr key=value,key=value,... \n
        Exclude records whose encoding contains any of the listed key/value pairs.
 \n \n --is_mtg2_switch 0|1|2 \n
        Restrict GRIB2 records to lte33=0, def=1, chemsplit=2.
 \n \n --edition 1|2 \n
        Restrict to GRIB edition 1 or 2.
 \n \n --show-encoding \n
        Print encoding key/value constraints for each result.
 \n \n --show-sources \n
        Print source definition files contributing to each result.
 \n \n --format line|table \n
        Output format. Default is line.
 \n \n --order asc|desc \n
        Sort order. Default is asc. Without --order-by, records are sorted by
        edition, MTG2 switch, scope and paramId.
 \n \n --order-by field1,field2,... \n
        Sort fields in priority order.
        Valid fields: edition,is_mtg2_switch,scope,paramId,shortName,name,units
 \n \n --no-truncate \n
        With --format table, do not truncate cells to the terminal width.
 \n \n
\section grib_parameters_examples grib_parameters examples
-# List all entries for paramId 130:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --paramId 130
\endverbatim

-# Show encoding constraints for exact WMO temperature triplet in GRIB2:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --edition 2 --attr discipline=0,parameterCategory=0,parameterNumber=0 --attr-strict --show-encoding
\endverbatim

-# Show only selected columns in table format:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --name '*temperature*' --columns edition,scope,paramId,shortName,encoding --format table
\endverbatim

-# Parameters of one centre, as used with the MTG2 switch set to 1:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --scope grib2/localConcepts/ecmf --is_mtg2_switch 1
\endverbatim

-# GRIB2 parameters with a statistical process, sorted by shortName:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --edition 2 --attrkey typeOfStatisticalProcessing --order-by shortName
\endverbatim

-# List all entries, then only encodings shared by several paramIds:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --format line
grib_parameters --format line | grep 'paramId=\['
\endverbatim

-# Check which definitions are read:\n
\verbatim
grib_parameters --paramId 167 --debug-path-resolution
\endverbatim
*/
